Add --lod-scale: draw only the shapes Haiku would draw at a given size

Haiku icons can have shapes that are visible only in a range of render
scales (size / 64), for example a simplified outline used at 16x16.
SVGWriter used to keep only the shapes visible at the largest size.
The new lodScale option (SVG and PNG, icon2icon --lod-scale) applies the
same rule as Haiku's PathSourceShape::Visible(). The default of 4 keeps
the old behavior.

Maintained in this repository; not part of upstream hvif-tools.

